This is a Material-UI v4.11.0 bug, not misuse. `OutlinedInput` passes `inputRef` to custom `inputComponent`s, but `TextareaAutosize` forwards that unknown prop to its underlying `<textarea>`.

Upgrade `@material-ui/core` to at least **4.11.1** (ideally the final v4 release, 4.12.4). The fix was to make `TextareaAutosize` consume `inputRef`.

```bash
npm install @material-ui/core@4.12.4
```

As a temporary workaround, wrap it and map `inputRef` to `ref`:

```jsx
const AutosizeInput = React.forwardRef(function AutosizeInput(props, ref) {
  const { inputRef, ...other } = props;

  return <TextareaAutosize {...other} ref={inputRef || ref} />;
});

<OutlinedInput inputComponent={AutosizeInput} />
```

`inputComponent` custom components must handle MUI’s input ref instead of passing `inputRef` through to a DOM element.
